    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Solanum torvum」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanum_torvum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1344107128,
      "text": "Solanum torvum, also known as pendejera, turkey berry, devil's fig, pea eggplant, platebrush or susumber, is a bushy, erect and spiny perennial plant used horticulturally as a rootstock for eggplant. Grafted plants are very vigorous and tolerate diseases affecting the root system, thus allowing the crop to continue for a second year."
    }
  },
